DICOMFall third-party notices
=============================

DICOMFall's own code is MIT (LICENSE). It builds on the work below, each under its own
license. The Linux image the game boots is downloaded and assembled by
`pnpm vm:image` from the pinned, checksummed files listed in
packages/machine/scripts/vm-image/vm-image.lock.json.

In the Linux image
------------------

- go-dicom, the released linux/386 binary (MIT), https://github.com/amrshadid/go-dicom
  Its own third-party notices are published with each release.
- Alpine Linux packages, each under its own license, as Alpine records it in the
  package's metadata. Among them: the Linux kernel (linux-virt, GPL-2.0-only), BusyBox
  (GPL-2.0-only), bash and readline (GPL-3.0-or-later), iproute2 (GPL-2.0-or-later),
  tcpdump and libpcap (BSD-3-Clause), ncurses (MIT-like). The exact versions are in the
  lock file. Their source code is available from Alpine Linux:
  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports and https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/
- SeaBIOS and the v86 BIOS images (LGPL-3.0), shipped by v86.

